## Round 2 – Refine the patch (same root‑cause, no public contract changes)

### 2️⃣ What the extra constraint means
* **Public message contracts must stay exactly the same.**  
  We cannot add new fields to any `ServerMessage` or `ClientMessage` type, nor can we change the shape of any existing payload.  
* The fix therefore has to be **internal only** – we can add new private fields or change the logic inside `GameRuntimeServer`, but the JSON that goes over the wire must remain untouched.

### 2️⃣ Why the original fix is still insufficient
The previous “else { return; }” in `restoreSession()` left the server in a half‑initialized state:

* `threadIds.gameplayByAgentId` stayed empty → the scheduler never sees any agent that has a thread.  
* `agentConfigs` stayed empty → later `requestGameplayTurn` would look up a model/effort for an agent that does not exist.  
* The simulation was created with a **seed of 0** (the default) even when the saved snapshot contained a different seed, breaking reproducibility.

All of those problems are **logic errors**, not protocol violations, so they can be fixed without touching any message schema.

### 2️⃣ Smallest safe internal fix

We will:

1. **Always guarantee a seed** – if the saved snapshot has no `seed` (or the seed is missing), generate a fresh one (exactly the same way `resetSession` does).  
2. **Always create at least one gameplay agent** – even when the snapshot contains no agents, we create a minimal agent (`agent-1`) with the (possibly newly‑generated) seed.  
3. **Reuse the existing `resetAgentLoopState` path** – after we have a seed and at least one agent we call the same helper that `resetSession` uses, so all internal maps (`actionQueueByAgent`, `godQueueByAgent`, …) are correctly primed.  
4. **Do not change any public type or message shape** – we only add a private helper and a few lines inside `restoreSession()`.

#### New private helper (added near the top of the class – does not affect the public API)

```ts
/** Create a minimal simulation + agent set when the saved snapshot is incomplete.
 *  This mirrors the logic in `resetSession` but keeps the existing seed (or creates a new one)
 *  and always returns a fully‑initialized state. */
private initFromScratch(seed: number): void {
  // Use the same world size as the rest of the codebase
  const content = this.contentStore.getContent();

  // Create a single placeholder agent – the same as `resetSession` does.
  this.simulation = new Simulation(
    seed,
    DEFAULT_WORLD_SIZE,
    DEFAULT_WORLD_SIZE,
    content,
    [{ id: "agent-1", name: "Agent 1" }]
  );

  this.seed = seed;
  this.agentConfigs.set("agent-1", { id: "agent-1", name: "Agent 1" });
  this.resetAgentLoopState(["agent-1"]);

  // No threads are restored – they will be (re)created by the normal start‑up flow.
  this.threadIds = { gameplayByAgentId: {} };
  this.threadToAgentId.clear();
  this.activeTurn = null;
  this.schedulerIndex = 0;
  this.interruptedTurnIds.clear();
  this.pendingTurns.clear();
  this.reasoningBuffers.clear();
}
```

