## Round 3 – Final patch plan (no new public contracts)

### 1️⃣ Goal
Make the **restore path** robust so that a persisted session is always usable, **without** changing any public message contract (`ServerMessage` / `ClientMessage`).  
The only allowed changes are internal – new private fields, helper methods, or refactored logic inside `GameRuntimeServer`.

### 2️⃣ Root cause (already identified)
`restoreSession()` can return early (`return;`) when the saved snapshot contains neither a `simulation` nor a numeric `seed`.  
When that happens the server stays in a half‑initialized state:

* `threadIds.gameplayByAgentId` is empty → scheduler never finds a runnable agent.  
* `agentConfigs` is empty → later `requestGameplayTurn` cannot resolve a model/effort.  
* The simulation may be created with the wrong seed (or with seed 0) and with no agents.

### 3️⃣ Minimal internal fix (no contract change)

#### 3.1 Add a private helper – `initFromScratch(seed: number)`

*Creates a minimal, fully‑initialized world when the saved snapshot is incomplete.*  
It mirrors the logic used in `resetSession` but keeps the supplied `seed` (or generates a fresh one) and always calls `resetAgentLoopState` so every internal map is populated.

```ts
/** Internal – initialise a fresh world when the saved snapshot is unusable.
 *  Guarantees:
 *   - a non‑null simulation,
 *   - a valid seed,
 *   - at least one gameplay agent (agent‑1),
 *   - all internal queues/maps cleared and primed.
 */
private initFromScratch(seed: number): void {
  const content = this.contentStore.getContent();

  // Create a single placeholder agent – same shape as resetSession does.
  this.simulation = new Simulation(
    seed,
    DEFAULT_WORLD_SIZE,
    DEFAULT_WORLD_SIZE,
    content,
    [{ id: "agent-1", name: "Agent 1" }]
  );

  this.seed = seed;
  this.agentConfigs.set("agent-1", { id: "agent-1", name: "Agent 1" });
  this.resetAgentLoopState(["agent-1"]);

  // No threads are restored here – the normal start‑up flow will create them.
  this.threadIds = { gameplayByAgentId: {} };
  this.threadToAgentId.clear();
  this.activeTurn = null;
  this.schedulerIndex = 0;
  this.interruptedTurnIds.clear();
  this.pendingTurns.clear();
  this.reasoningBuffers.clear();
}
```

*No new fields are added to the public state; everything is private to the class.*

#### 3.2 Refactor `restoreSession()`

Replace the final `else { return; }` with a call to `initFromScratch`.  
Also guarantee that a numeric seed is always present (the saved snapshot may have a non‑numeric `seed` or none at all).

